in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @cascade
in @labeled
in @facet/rust
in @facet/llvm

# @cascade/code/rust/llvm — the Rust → LLVM IR cascade species.
#
# Path naming: per Alex 2026-06-23 directive — cascade species
# shards group by `@cascade/code/<source>/<target>`. Source
# language (Rust) groups together; targets (llvm here; wasm at
# the sibling `shards/cascade/code/rust/wasm.mirror`) are leaves.
#
# THIS species is Edge 1 of the concrete polyglot chain Alex
# ratified 2026-07-17 (verbatim, session-crystallizing):
#
#   *"So we can have @cascade/code/llvm/turing and
#    @cascade/code/rust/llvm. And boom. The loop closes."*
#
# The full chain per polyglot spec §4.1 (Mara `1ce68c3`,
# 2026-07-17):
#
#   Rust source
#     ↓  @cascade/code/rust/llvm      (THIS shard; shells to
#                                       rustc --emit=llvm-ir)
#   LLVM IR
#     ↓  @cascade/code/llvm/turing    (sibling mint this tick)
#   Turing tape
#     ↓  @cascade/code/turing/mirror  (sibling mint this tick)
#   mirror substrate composition
#
# === substrate-already-had-the-word ===
#
# The rustc `--emit=llvm-ir` capability is upstream-landed
# tooling since 2015; the substrate does NOT re-implement it. The
# `apply_rust_llvm` action shells to it at @io boundary per
# `[[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]`. `bootstrap/src/lib.rs`
# ALREADY carries the plumbing for shelling to rustc (per polyglot
# spec §5 loss-aware note); THIS shard names the substrate-decl
# the FLOOR resolver (Reed Tick M3 domain) discharges against.
#
# === composition altitude: SOURCE-ADJACENT ===
#
# The source altitude is `@facet/rust` (landed
# `shards/code/rust.mirror`). The target altitude is `@facet/llvm`
# (landed `shards/code/llvm.mirror` this session; Mara M1
# `62d1b1c`). This species is the ADJACENT-ALTITUDE morphism
# between them; per polyglot spec §3.2 composition axiom, it
# composes with `@cascade/code/llvm/turing` (sibling mint) to
# give O(N)-authored coverage of O(N²) translation pairs through
# the @facet/llvm machine-substrate hub.
#
# === The cascade shape (Rust → LLVM IR) ===
#
# Source (Rust admits):
# - lifetimes (ownership tracking; erased at monomorphization)
# - generics (monomorphized at compile time; erased)
# - trait objects (partial preservation via vtable; most erased)
# - macros (expanded before IR emission; source-level erased)
# - type inference decisions (elaborated to concrete types)
# - borrow-checker proofs (used to gate emission; not preserved
#   as data in the LLVM IR output)
#
# Target (LLVM IR preserves per LangRef):
# - typed SSA values (LLVM's type system per LangRef §"Type
#   System"; concrete after monomorphization)
# - control flow (basic blocks + terminators per LangRef
#   §"Terminator Instructions"; structured after Rust's
#   surface control flow is lowered)
# - function signatures (typed; calling convention annotated)
# - attributes (function/parameter attributes per LangRef
#   §"Function Attributes"; some Rust safety info preserved
#   as attributes e.g. `noalias`, `nonnull`)
# - metadata (debug info, TBAA, loop hints; optional)
# - target datalayout + triple (bound at compile time)
#
# Per polyglot spec §4.4 Edge 1:
# - PRESERVED: types (via LLVM type system), function
#   signatures, control flow (structured), basic operations.
# - LOST: lifetimes (erased at monomorphization), generics
#   (monomorphized), macros (expanded), trait objects (partial
#   via vtables), high-level ownership discipline.
#
# The `loss_lens<@facet/rust, @facet/llvm>` measures these gaps
# against the rustc emission + the LLVM LangRef target grammar.
#
# === Recognition ancestry ===
#
# - Recognition #95 (@cascade candidate; Mara canonical
#   `ce4874b`, 2026-06-23): this species IS one of the cascade
#   species discharging the family-root.
# - Recognition #93 H4 RESOLVED (labeled<> functor at
#   `shards/labeled.mirror`): llvm_artifact uses labeled<>
#   instance for module + emission metadata.
# - Recognition #51 (mirror as expanding Hilbert space): the
#   dimension-projection from Rust's typed-feature surface to
#   LLVM's typed-SSA surface is measurable via
#   `measure_rust_llvm`.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   rustc --emit=llvm-ir     Rust Project 2015-present; the
#                            canonical rustc flag that emits LLVM
#                            IR at any compilation stage. Load-
#                            bearing external tooling this species
#                            dispatches at @io boundary.
#   LLVM LangRef             LLVM Project; llvm.org/docs/
#                            LangRef.html. The target grammar
#                            this species measures against.
#   Alive2                   Lopes et al. 2021; translation-
#                            validation research grounding
#                            per-instruction semantic-preservation
#                            proofs; the empirical shape the
#                            loss-lens references.
#   MIR (Rust)               Rust Project 2016-present; the
#                            mid-level IR rustc lowers to before
#                            LLVM emission. Rust's source-level
#                            information is progressively erased
#                            through HIR → MIR → LLVM IR; this
#                            species measures the terminal-hop
#                            erasure.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/polyglot-loss-aware-computational-
#               translation.md §4.1 + §4.2 Edge 1 + §9 M2 (Mara
#               `1ce68c3`, 2026-07-17 — the mint plan
#               forward-promise THIS shard discharges); §4.4
#               Edge 1 preservation/loss enumeration; §5 loss-
#               aware note on rustc `--emit=llvm-ir` as the
#               FLOOR dispatch target.
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]] (the
#                      lift is LLVM LangRef + rustc emission
#                      contract; NOT re-derived at substrate),
#                      [[feedback-loss-from-epistemologic-properties]]
#                      (loss is @epistemologic/properties composite,
#                      not Shannon, not invented),
#                      [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] (every action
#                      body `\` blocked; FLOOR realisation domain).
# Related shards: shards/cascade.mirror (the family-root this
#                 specializes); shards/labeled.mirror (the functor
#                 primitive llvm_artifact instance rests on);
#                 shards/code/rust.mirror (source grammar);
#                 shards/code/llvm.mirror (target grammar; Mara
#                 M1 landed this session at `62d1b1c`);
#                 shards/cascade/code/rust/wasm.mirror (sibling
#                 dual-target species with same source);
#                 shards/cascade/code/llvm/turing.mirror (sibling
#                 mint this tick; composes with THIS species per
#                 polyglot spec §3.2 to give Rust → Turing via
#                 @facet/llvm hub).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/cascade/code/rust/llvm.mirror` declares
# `@cascade/code/rust/llvm` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming-languages/rust-2024-edition
source @arxiv/programming-languages/llvm-langref

prism @cascade/code/rust/llvm {
  focus cascade
  project cascade
  split cascade
  shift cascade
  settle cascade
}

# === rust_source carrier ===
#
# Specialization of @cascade.typed_source for source_grammar=rust.
# References a Rust crate (Cargo.toml + src/*) as the unit of
# cascade. SHARED SHAPE with the sibling
# `shards/cascade/code/rust/wasm.mirror` :123 rust_source carrier;
# intentional duplication at substrate-decl altitude — the property
# is the same and discharges identically across dual-target
# siblings.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the source-tree content hash.
type rust_source = ref

# === llvm_emission_metadata carrier ===
#
# Structured carrier for the rustc emission shape (target triple,
# optimization level, codegen units, LTO mode, debug info level,
# emission-time diagnostics). Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]:
# structured, not stringly. The carrier names load-bearing fields
# without fixing one rustc release shape; the FLOOR resolver
# (Reed Tick M3) populates concrete values from the invocation.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type llvm_emission_metadata = ref

# === llvm_artifact carrier ===
#
# The @labeled<> instance per recognition #93 H4. An llvm_artifact
# IS a `@facet/llvm.llvm_ir_module` annotated with
# llvm_emission_metadata via the labeled functor. Substrate-
# architecturally load-bearing: the module's typed identity is
# preserved (via labeled parametricity per Wadler 1989 / Reynolds
# 1983) while the emission-context dimension is added.
# `unlabel(artifact)` returns the module; `label_of(artifact)`
# returns the metadata.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the (module, metadata) pair
# (inherited from @labeled).
type llvm_artifact = labeled(llvm_ir_module, llvm_emission_metadata)

# === apply_rust_llvm action ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION. Specialization of @cascade.compile for
# the Rust → LLVM IR functor. Takes a rust_source; returns the
# `@facet/llvm.llvm_ir_module`.
#
# Realisation shells to `rustc --emit=llvm-ir` at the @io boundary
# (per polyglot spec §5 loss-aware note; bootstrap/src/lib.rs
# already carries the plumbing). The FLOOR resolver (Reed Tick M3
# under `[substrate-floor:@io-boundary]`) MUST discharge the body;
# THIS shard names the CONTRACT the FLOOR honors.
#
# Per Alex 2026-07-17 verbatim: *"So we can have @cascade/code/
# llvm/turing and @cascade/code/rust/llvm. And boom. The loop
# closes."* — this action IS the first edge that closes the loop.
#
# requires rust_well_typed(source, p): the substrate forecloses
# emission against type errors. rustc runs the typing discipline;
# the bilateral verdict reflects what it reports. (SHARED bilateral
# shape with the sibling rust/wasm cascade species per polyglot
# spec §4.2 Edge 1.)
#
# Body discharges at the FLOOR boundary.
apply_rust_llvm(source: rust_source, p: perturbation) -> llvm_ir_module
requires rust_well_typed(source, p)
{ \ }

# === bundle_llvm action ===
#
# Wraps an `llvm_ir_module` + `llvm_emission_metadata` into an
# `llvm_artifact` via @labeled.label construction. The typed
# module gets the emission-context dimension added without losing
# the underlying module identity.
#
# requires llvm_emission_coherent(module, metadata, p): bilateral
# commitment that the (module, metadata) pair coheres at the
# emission altitude — target triple matches datalayout;
# optimization level consistent with emitted attributes; debug
# info level matches emitted metadata nodes.
#
# Body discharges at the FLOOR boundary.
bundle_llvm(module: llvm_ir_module, metadata: llvm_emission_metadata, p: perturbation)
  -> llvm_artifact
requires llvm_emission_coherent(module, metadata, p)
{ \ }

# === measure_rust_llvm action ===
#
# Specialization of @cascade.measure for the Rust → LLVM IR
# cascade. Returns substrate-typed measurement of information
# loss between rust_source's typing/lifetime/generic/macro
# discipline and llvm_artifact's typed-SSA runtime-preserved
# structure.
#
# Returns `imperfect<llvm_artifact, ref, information_loss>` — the
# loss slot carries measured loss as substrate-typed data, NOT
# Shannon, NOT estimation; the composite of @epistemologic/
# properties per [[feedback-loss-from-epistemologic-properties]].
#
# The measurement IS substrate-architectural: read source's
# typing-discipline use (lifetime-annotation sites, generic
# parameter count, macro-invocation count, trait-object usage,
# borrow-checker proof density); read artifact's LLVM IR module
# structure (function signatures, basic-block graph, attribute
# annotations, metadata density); compute the dimension gap per
# polyglot spec §4.4 Edge 1.
#
# requires rust_llvm_loss_well_defined(source, artifact, p):
# bilateral that the measurement IS computable; the (source,
# artifact) pair must be a genuine cascade discharge (rustc
# emitted THIS module from THIS source).
#
# Body discharges at the FLOOR boundary.
measure_rust_llvm(source: rust_source, artifact: llvm_artifact, p: perturbation)
  -> imperfect(llvm_artifact, ref, information_loss)
requires rust_llvm_loss_well_defined(source, artifact, p)
{ \ }

# === rust_well_typed bilateral ===
#
# Source-side typing-discipline bilateral. Specializes the family-
# root's grammar_coherent at source_grammar=rust. SHARED shape
# with the sibling `shards/cascade/code/rust/wasm.mirror` :217
# rust_well_typed bilateral; intentional duplication at
# substrate-decl altitude — the property discharges identically
# regardless of downstream target choice (rustc's typer runs the
# same discipline for llvm and wasm emission).
#
# Splinter-pole: source passes rustc typecheck; borrow checker
# clears; trait bounds satisfied; monomorphization succeeds.
# Narcissus-pole: type errors OR lifetime errors OR unsatisfied
# trait bounds OR monomorphization failures. Emission cannot
# proceed.
rust_well_typed(source: rust_source, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === llvm_emission_coherent bilateral ===
#
# Target-side emission-well-formedness bilateral. Commitment that
# the (module, metadata) pair coheres at LLVM emission altitude.
#
# Splinter-pole: target triple matches datalayout; optimization
# level consistent with emitted attributes; debug info nodes
# match emission metadata; module passes LLVM Verifier
# (composes with `@facet/llvm.llvm_ir_valid` per Mara `62d1b1c`).
# Narcissus-pole: triple/datalayout mismatch; attributes drift
# from optimization level; debug info incoherent; Verifier
# rejects.

bilateral llvm_emission_coherent {
  sentinel "emission=triple-datalayout-attrs-coherent"
  arity 2
}
llvm_emission_coherent(module: llvm_ir_module, metadata: llvm_emission_metadata, p: perturbation)
  -> verdict { \ }

# === rust_llvm_loss_well_defined bilateral ===
#
# Specializes the family-root's loss_well_defined for this
# cascade. Commitment that the substrate-typed gap calculation IS
# computable for the (source, artifact) pair; the source IS in
# @facet/rust grammar, the artifact's module IS in @facet/llvm
# grammar, and the pair represents a valid cascade discharge
# (rustc `--emit=llvm-ir` produced THIS artifact from THIS source).
#
# Splinter-pole: cascade-pair coherent; measurement well-defined;
# gap dimensions dischargeable per @epistemologic/properties
# composite.
# Narcissus-pole: source/artifact grammar mismatch OR pair does
# not represent a genuine cascade discharge; measurement
# undefined.

bilateral rust_llvm_loss_well_defined {
  sentinel "cascade=source-artifact-pair-discharge-witnessed"
  arity 2
}
rust_llvm_loss_well_defined(source: rust_source, artifact: llvm_artifact, p: perturbation)
  -> verdict { \ }

# === cascade_rust_llvm_preserves_semantics bilateral ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING composed bilateral for THIS species. Witnesses
# that the Rust → LLVM IR cascade preserves runtime semantics per
# LLVM's translation guarantees (per polyglot spec §7 admissibility
# proof-sketch; Church-Turing grounding).
#
# Per Alex 2026-07-17 verbatim ratification (`1ce68c3` + this
# session's continuation): the cascade DOES lose Rust source-level
# information (comments, formatting, macro-expansion history,
# type-inference decisions, borrow-checker proofs); it PRESERVES
# runnable-semantics per LLVM's translation-validation research
# (Alive2 et al.). This bilateral names that split.
#
# Splinter-pole: LLVM IR module discharges the SAME runtime
# semantics as the Rust source per rustc's guarantee; loss is
# bounded to source-level dimensions (comments / formatting /
# macro-expansion-history / type-inference-decisions / borrow-
# checker-proofs); runnable execution preserves observable
# behaviour.
# Narcissus-pole: cascade drifts runtime semantics (rustc emission
# bug; LLVM datalayout mismatch; UB-triggering optimization
# introduced at emission); observable behaviour diverges between
# source and artifact.
#
# Sentinel `cascade=preserves-runnable-semantics` per Mara
# `701828a` §1 byte-containment: content-addressed check on the
# cascade-pair OID vs the preservation-witness invariant. Rice-
# safe per Mara `701828a` — the CHECK is byte-level; the
# underlying question (full semantic equivalence) is undecidable
# but the substrate discharges the sentinel-match at content-
# addressed altitude.

bilateral cascade_rust_llvm_preserves_semantics {
  sentinel "cascade=preserves-runnable-semantics"
  arity 1
}
cascade_rust_llvm_preserves_semantics(cascade_outcome: llvm_artifact) -> verdict { \ }

# === rust_llvm_cascade_well_formed composed bilateral ===
#
# Specialization of @cascade.cascade_well_defined for this cascade
# instance. Composes the sub-predicates at this altitude per the
# landed cascade composed-bilateral shape (rust/wasm :268,
# gleam/beam, etc.).
#
# requires rust_well_typed(source, p): source-side typing
# discipline coherent.
# requires llvm_emission_coherent(unlabel(artifact, p),
# label_of(artifact, p), p): target-side emission well-formed;
# uses @labeled.unlabel + @labeled.label_of to extract module
# and metadata from the artifact.
# requires rust_llvm_loss_well_defined(source, artifact, p):
# loss measurement computable.
# requires cascade_rust_llvm_preserves_semantics(artifact):
# runtime-semantics preservation witnessed at cascade altitude.
#
# All four must hold; substrate refuses cascade if source has
# type errors OR emission incoherent OR loss undefined OR
# semantics-preservation not witnessed.
#
# Splinter-pole: all four discharge; substrate-typed loss
# returned; cascade admissible per polyglot spec §5.3
# threshold gate.
# Narcissus-pole: at least one sub-predicate fails; cascade
# blocked; @fate re-selects per polyglot spec §6.

bilateral rust_llvm_cascade_well_formed {
  sentinel "cascade=all-sub-bilaterals-discharge"
  arity 2
}
rust_llvm_cascade_well_formed(source: rust_source, artifact: llvm_artifact, p: perturbation)
  -> verdict
requires rust_well_typed(source, p)
requires llvm_emission_coherent(unlabel(artifact, p), label_of(artifact, p), p)
requires rust_llvm_loss_well_defined(source, artifact, p)
requires cascade_rust_llvm_preserves_semantics(artifact)
{ \ }

# === outbound declarations ===

out @cascade/code/rust/llvm
out rust_source
out llvm_emission_metadata
out llvm_artifact
out apply_rust_llvm
out bundle_llvm
out measure_rust_llvm
out rust_well_typed
out llvm_emission_coherent
out rust_llvm_loss_well_defined
out cascade_rust_llvm_preserves_semantics
out rust_llvm_cascade_well_formed
